{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1386711-non-goth-hollow-ones-just-asking","id":1386711,"title":"Non goth hollow ones. Just asking","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-08T09:11:49-07:00","id":1386711,"title":"Non goth hollow ones. Just asking","content":"What are non-goth hollow ones like? I've read the novel with Penny Dreadful but would kinda like a better view of things. It's a bit in relation to my wondering and someone's question in a previous post of if Hollow ones are a thing in the Philippines, if that helps any.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T09:18:23-07:00","id":1386716,"title":"","content":"A Non-Goth Hollow One is just about any Hollow One under the age of 40. LoL<br /> Or over 20. Among the youth, the Goth fashion has made a slight comeback the last two years.<br /> IMO, this game needs to shake free from that old fashioned Gothic Punk theme. It is very retro and dated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T12:31:29-07:00","id":1386754,"title":"","content":"Okay... Uh. So... What are they like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T12:50:03-07:00","id":1386763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1386711-non-goth-hollow-ones-just-asking?p=1386754#post1386754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay... Uh. So... What are they like?</div> </div> </div> </div>Effectively, I would suggest that the Hollow Ones have never been Goths exclusively. They're a disparate (ha!) group of DIY dime-store magicians that are the &quot;mish mash&quot; paradigm. It's just that teenagers in the World of Darkness are morbid and punk-ish people so they tend to look like Goths. If you want an idea of what they're like just imagine any mage that has a kitchen sink paradigm.<br /> <br /> * Laptop to communicate with the dead<br /> * College notebook of spells<br /> * Blood sacrifice dagger<br /> * Taser of lightning<br /> * Harry Potter Wand<br /> * Slytherin Scarf<br /> * Chemistry notebooks<br /> <br /> They see no reason to stick to one paradigm and live on the margins of magickal society. Their group exists solely so they don't get picked off one by one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T13:04:00-07:00","id":1386769,"title":"","content":"Check out the revised tradition book, they have examples in the back of non goth hollows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T13:14:36-07:00","id":1386771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1386711-non-goth-hollow-ones-just-asking?p=1386769#post1386769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Check out the revised tradition book, they have examples in the back of non goth hollows.</div> </div> </div> </div>I recommend OUTCASTS instead of the Tradition Books for the Hollow Ones.<br /> <br /> It's really good for making them solid protagonists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T13:59:17-07:00","id":1386774,"title":"","content":"I recommend Outcasts as well. Hollow Ones were created as a faction during Mage 1st edition. Unless you put in a little work, the assumption was that Goths were the non-Tradition mages and non-Technocracy and non-Marauders.<br /> <br /> With M20, since how you do magick is personal, there's not a need for the Hollow Ones except as a group that has some shared practices and bands together for mutual benefit.<br /> <br /> As for countries outside the U.S., I'm not familiar enough with their culture to really suggest whether the particular Hollow One ideas in the book work there. . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T14:45:08-07:00","id":1386781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baakyocalder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1386711-non-goth-hollow-ones-just-asking?p=1386774#post1386774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I recommend Outcasts as well. Hollow Ones were created as a faction during Mage 1st edition. Unless you put in a little work, the assumption was that Goths were the non-Tradition mages and non-Technocracy and non-Marauders.<br /> <br /> With M20, since how you do magick is personal, there's not a need for the Hollow Ones except as a group that has some shared practices and bands together for mutual benefit.<br /> <br /> As for countries outside the U.S., I'm not familiar enough with their culture to really suggest whether the particular Hollow One ideas in the book work there. . .</div> </div> </div> </div>The tone of the two books are also very different and more akin to what the OP wants I think.<br /> <br /> 1. OUTCASTS treats the Hollow Ones as a bunch of dark Byronic romantics as well as runaways, outcasts, and cynics about the Ascension War. It's mostly a Craft that is struggling for survival and wants nothing to do with the conflict but will defend itself against the Union if push comes to shove. It also will leave them alone if they get left alone. The Goth element is not that important since a few are over a century old.<br /> <br /> 2. The Tradition book for Revised doubles and triples down on the Goth element. They take on Goth names like Circe Nightshade and emphasize the clubs, fashion, and the fact that they're imitating people from pop culture like Johnny Depp's Sleepy Hollow or Jedi. They are wholly and completely ridiculous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T18:10:46-07:00","id":1386848,"title":"","content":"I'd advise looking into the Revised Tradition book as well because while it does certainly have fun with the goth vibes and aesthetics it also lays out why some Hollow Ones are goths but not all.<br /> <br /> The Hollow One paradigm isn't about poetry, wearing black, or velvet-clad sensualist seducing shades of the dead; although it can accommodate all of these things.<br /> <br /> The Hollow One paradigm is, put in two words, Optimistic Nihilism. They are what a well-adjusted person would become instead of a Nephandus after the same revelation.<br /> <br /> The Hollow One paradigm is built upon the realization that life is ultimately meaningless and that we are but crude clay screaming into the abyss for a few decades and composed of simple elements that spend our whole lives breaking down and then fading away.<br /> <br /> Life has no intrinsic meaning. The cosmos is unfeeling and uncaring. Their is no G-D or any other divine being. We are simply the scions of the accident of sentience.<br /> <br /> Yet, Hollow Ones realize this and as they waken they do not despair; they rejoice. Life has no intrinsic meaning. Life has no 'true' purpose. That means that everything we do in life is ultimately our own choice and there's something unspeakably beautiful and awe-inspiring about that to a Hollower.<br /> <br /> We live for ourselves. Our times on this world are brief flecks before nonexistence. The fact that the world has no meaning is miraculous because that means all meaning is what we create for ourselves.<br /> <br /> There is no cosmic judge! There is no balance of forced! God is dead! Live and do as you please, rejoice for you are free!<br /> <br /> Hollowers create their own meanings and live passionately as they choose to live because those meanings are beautiful in the face of the one truth that there is no truth. Hollowers live freely and passionately as themselves.<br /> <br /> You want to be the next Byron? Write sister! Wear black, get drunk on absinthe, seduce Death! You want to be a pirate? Wear frilly shirts and high boots and rock it brother! You want to recreate Roman fashion in your garage and live as a weary but honorable plebeian? Ave Roma! <br /> <br /> The Hollowers take their name from the joking statement of one of their founders, who raised his glass and observed that we are all empty and that what we our is what we fill ourselves with.<br /> <br /> So, rejoice!<br /> <br /> We are Hollow Men!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T19:17:45-07:00","id":1386866,"title":"","content":"Some teens today are still goth, but usually not to the ridiculous extent shown in Revised (even my friend who\u2019s really into MM isn\u2019t that bad). But I think a lot of mages of all ages are still drawn to the Hollow Ones\u2019 sense of romance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T19:24:20-07:00","id":1386871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1386711-non-goth-hollow-ones-just-asking?p=1386781#post1386781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The tone of the two books are also very different and more akin to what the OP wants I think.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. The combination of those two books is kind of what confused me to begin with. The Tradition book seems to suggest some sort of be necessary goth like qualities and then adds in some weirdness while the outcast one seems to be about them. So I was kind of wondering what their group culture was like to see if anything quite like it or signs of it exist in my country.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T19:37:04-07:00","id":1386876,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11637_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11637\" data-vbnamecard=\"11637\">Gryffon15</a> That helps a lot.<br /> <br /> I'm guessing that's their uniting factor, Optimistic Nihilism and the passion to live exactly as they want without worrying too much about fitting in. <br /> <br /> So follow up question: in your opinion, how would you hypothetically go looking for them in different countries you are familiar with? What would you look for? How would you, say, differentiate a hollower group from just a bunch of mages with eclectic magickal practice without having to know them personally?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T19:55:23-07:00","id":1386880,"title":"","content":"No worries! The Hollow Ones are maybe my favorite tradition/craft and I'm happy to share my reasons and appreciation!<br /> <br /> Going to look for Hollowers is a bit difficult because of how incredibly diverse they can be but there are some common trends. They do tend to congregate and cliques sometimes form between them with trends usually involve nightlife, music culture, and other various subcultures. I'd advise really trying to look in places where such things gather with the help of Prime. The differences are sometimes academic as the Hollowers are something of a tradition of Orphans. The main common trend is the philosophy of Optimistic Nihilism while orphans really do just depend on the tastes on the associated Willworkers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T20:04:33-07:00","id":1386883,"title":"","content":"So independent and alternative music scene would maybe be a good place to find them in like any country? (I am trying to place them as a Storyteller)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":".  Typo 05-08-2020, 11:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T22:19:28-07:00","id":1386911,"title":"","content":"Here's an irony: up until M20, what M20 now calls Gutter Magic was near-universal among both Hollow Ones and Orphans. In M20, that's explicitly still the case for Hollow Ones; but for Orphans, it's merely \u201cespecially prevalent\u201d. That is, an M20 Orphan is significantly less likely to practice Gutter Magic than an M20 Hollow One is. Heck, it's even entirely possible that the majority of M20 Orphans <i>don't</i> practice Gutter Magic. <br /> <br /> But the Hollow Ones? They positively take <i>pride</i> in their practice of Gutter Magic; it is to them what Witchcraft is to the Verbena, Crazy Wisdom is to the Cult of Ecstasy, and High Ritual is to the Order of Hermes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T09:36:25-07:00","id":1386992,"title":"","content":"My own take on the Hollow Ones evolved over the years. At some point around 15 or so years ago, I realized that their overall philosophy can best be summed up as &quot;It is what it is.&quot; Which is to say, they recognized the World of Darkness and its Gothic Punk theme-mood<sup>1</sup> for what it is, and meet it head on. The world is a strange and sometimes scary place, full of weirdness and mystery, and because of that, it is not only pretty cool at times, but also a source of secrets and power. They also frequently try to appear cynical and world-weary, as though they've seen it all and bought the t-shirt, because it makes them look more knowledgable and less impacted by some of the darker things they've seen. But at heart, they tend to be romantics (although sometimes damaged ones), who see things that evoke a very strong emotional response and deep inside their hearts go &quot;neat!&quot;<br /> They tend to gravitate toward romantic leaning subcultures, and this goes back a long ways. At least to the 18th century, with its Sturm und Drang movement, Gothic novel development, Hellfire Clubs, and other aspects of the Romantic period of art and literature, as well as aspects of the First Great Awakening. But also 19th century things like the Bohemian movements, European nationalist movements, artist colonies, spiritualism, and the Grand Guignol. In the 20th century, this runs through cabarets, the Lost Generation, 1940s hipsters, the Beats, hot rod and motorcycle culture, Mods, early rockers, outlaw country, Glams, metal heads, punks, Goths, grunge, and various forms of hip hop.<br /> And that's just the Euro-American part of them. Places like Japan or South Africa are going to have their own takes based on visual kei, bosozoku, delinquent, Smarteez, afrometal, and swenkas, among other things. Mexican or Mexican-American Hollowers may opt for stylistic influences from, say, La Calavera Catrina or masked luchadors mythology in addition to the usual gotico, metalero, and other tribus urbanas. And so on around the globe. <br /> <br /> I'm not entirely up on modern Filipino culture, but I suspect at least one home/outlet for local Hollow Ones is in Manila's underground punk/DIY scene detailed in Jess Khol's 2018 short documentary <a href=\"https://youtu.be/BtSZt_KeiGU\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Anarchy in the Philippines</b></a>. <br /> <br /> My own two part post about internal factions and subfactions I use for the Hollow Ones is <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1360544-homebrew-headcanons?p=1377604#post1377604\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1360544-homebrew-headcanons?p=1377622#post1377622\">here</a>. <br /> <br /> <sup>1</sup>And what I mean by Gothic-Punk as a theme and mood can be found about halfway through <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1382386-general-headcanons?p=1382408#post1382408\">this post</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T09:44:22-07:00","id":1386995,"title":"","content":"Thanks everyone and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12890_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12890\" data-vbnamecard=\"12890\">No One of Consequence</a>! That helps a lot!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T12:52:13-07:00","id":1387051,"title":"","content":"Goth is still a huge thing in Germany and never died out there. Sort of like how America decided DISCO SUCKS while everyone else just went on with it and it became House Music.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-09-2020, 05:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T14:07:56-07:00","id":1387076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1386711-non-goth-hollow-ones-just-asking?p=1387051#post1387051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Goth is still a huge thing in Germany and never died out there. Sort of like how America decided DISCO SUCKS while everyone else just went on with it and he became House Music.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's kind of the same way that in the 90s, most of the good heavy metal music was coming from Europe and other places.<br /> <br /> Added: Which reminds me, one of my guilty pleasures is a 1986 film, <i>Trick or Treat</i>, about a teen metal head who is able to summon the damned soul of his deceased idol by playing his last album backwards. It's a weird but fun film, though the lip syncing is some of the worst committed to film, and I've used it as inspiration for a Hollower character who Awakened in the same circumstances, with the dead rock star being his Avatar, and learning various rotes and other tricks by finding rare pressings of various hard rock and metal albums and playing them backwards to unlock their secrets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 05-09-2020, 06:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}